# CQ 22: Which user data does a communication carry, and through which
# protocol data unit?
#
# The chain from a communication to its payload: a communication transmits a
# protocol data unit, 5.6.1 splits that unit into control information and user
# data, and the user data is what the sender actually wanted to send.
#
# The question exists for the alignment. aias:carriesData starts at exactly
# this user data and reaches the dataset of the ISO/IEC 22989 pattern, so a
# model can ask which communications carry a given dataset. The chain has to be
# walkable from this end for that to work.
#
# The control information is reported alongside, since a unit carrying only
# control information and no user data is a legitimate case: an acknowledgement
# conveys no payload.
PREFIX iso7498: <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso7498#>
SELECT ?communication ?pdu ?userData ?controlInformation ?layerNumber
WHERE {
  ?communication iso7498:transmits ?pdu .
  ?pdu a iso7498:ProtocolDataUnit .
  OPTIONAL { ?pdu iso7498:hasUserData ?userData }
  OPTIONAL { ?pdu iso7498:hasControlInformation ?controlInformation }
  OPTIONAL { ?pdu iso7498:atLayer/iso7498:layerNumber ?layerNumber }
} ORDER BY ?communication ?pdu
